  I normally use 11s to search (search eleven times unless/until 
something is found).  On the early levels this may have to be repeated
three (3) times before a hidden door is found.  That's a minimum
of 23 searches.

  If it's the same for traps then it may not be possible to find all 
traps.   It's only used when I'm sure there's a secret door there, or
the downstairs cannot be found.

  When the downstairs can't be found, search for hidden doors with 
"11s".  Then move three steps along the wall, then search "11s" again.
Since the search command searches all 8 surrounding squares this will
prevent double-searching of squares.

